14256.sol:
V=100 $\text{ volt }$ Given, $\lambda_0=de-Broglie wavelength of $proton \therefore \quad \lambda_0=$\frac{h}{\sqrt{2 m_p q_p V}}$ de-Broglie wavelength of $\alpha$-particle $\begin{aligned}
\lambda& =\frac{h}{\sqrt{2 m_\alpha q_\alpha V}}\\
m_\alpha \text{$ and $}  =4 m_p
\end{aligned} (Mass of \alpha$-particle is four times of proton) q_\alpha=2 q_p (Charge of \alpha-particle is twice of $proton) \begin{aligned}
