63384.sol:
$\tan \alpha$ and $\tan \beta$ are roots of the $a x^2-b x y-y^2=0
\begin{aligned}& \therefore \tan \alpha+\tan \beta=\frac{-(-\mathrm{b})}{-1}=-\mathrm{b} \text{$ and $} \tan \alpha \tan \beta=\frac{\mathrm{a}}{(-1)}=-\mathrm{a}\\ \text{ and } \tan (\alpha+\beta)=\frac{\tan \alpha+\tan \beta}{1-\tan \alpha \tan \beta}=\frac{-\mathrm{b}}{1-(-\mathrm{a})}=\frac{-\mathrm{b}}{1+\mathrm{a}}
